IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gdpr-core`
IMPORT `gdpr-core-2`

-- ============================================================================
-- gdpr-definitions-2.l4 -- ARTICLE 4 LEAD-IN AND POINTS (3), (4), (5), (9) TO (26) OF REGULATION (EU) 2016/679.
-- Part of the keel, written by K2 (Sonnet 5.5).  Points (1), (2), (6), (7), (8) are P1's, in gdpr-definitions.l4.
-- One function per defined term (a sub-point that has its own question has its own function); the arguments
-- are facts a person could state.  Imports gdpr-core.l4 and gdpr-core-2.l4; never edits them.
--
-- ANSWERS.  Every decision function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN or MAYBE of an enumeration; the two exceptions
-- are the regulative rule of Art 4(9) (a DEONTIC) and `Art 4(13) to (15) the categories ...` (a MAYBE LIST).
-- JUST FALSE is given only where the definition says "means" (or a flat negative); each such branch carries
-- a FALSE-kind comment and each NOTHING branch a NOTHING-kind comment (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed,
-- not ruled).  An argument that the text declares irrelevant ("whether or not", "in particular", "such as")
-- is kept so that the clause has a test, and says so in a comment.
--
-- BORROWED FACTS.  Where a definition leans on a provision of another part (Article 27 for 'representative',
-- Article 51 for 'supervisory authority') or on another instrument (Directive (EU) 2015/1535 for
-- 'information society service'), the fact is asked as a plain BOOLEAN input and the other provision is not
-- encoded here.
-- ============================================================================

§ `Article 4: the lead-in`

-- src:36 | Article 4
-- src:37 | Definitions
-- src:38 | For the purposes of this Regulation:
@ref Art 4 'Definitions', lead-in (src:36-38)
GIVEN `the term is used for the purposes of this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4 lead-in the definitions of Article 4 apply to the term` MEANS
    IF `the term is used for the purposes of this Regulation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of this Regulation:" says nothing of a use of the term outside this Regulation

§ `Article 4(3): restriction of processing`

-- src:41 | (3) ‘restriction of processing’ means the marking of stored personal data with the aim of limiting their processing in the future;
@ref Art 4(3) 'restriction of processing' (src:41)
GIVEN `the personal data are stored` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal data are marked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aim of the marking is to limit the processing of the personal data in the future` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(3) the act is a restriction of processing` MEANS
    IF `the personal data are stored` AND `the personal data are marked` AND `the aim of the marking is to limit the processing of the personal data in the future`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means the marking of stored personal data with the aim of limiting their processing in the future"

§ `Article 4(4): profiling`

-- src:42 | (4) ‘profiling’ means any form of automated processing of personal data consisting of the use of personal data to evaluate certain personal aspects relating to a natural person, in particular to analyse or predict aspects concerning that natural person's performance at work, economic situation, health, personal preferences, interests, reliability, behaviour, location or movements;
@ref Art 4(4) 'profiling' (src:42)
GIVEN `the processing is processing of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is automated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal aspects that the personal data are used to evaluate` IS A LIST OF `Art 4(4) personal aspect`
      `the aspects relate to a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(4) the processing is profiling` MEANS
    IF `the processing is processing of personal data`
       AND `the processing is automated`
       AND NOT (null `the personal aspects that the personal data are used to evaluate`)
       AND `the aspects relate to a natural person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any form of automated processing of personal data consisting of the use of personal data to evaluate certain personal aspects relating to a natural person"
    -- "in particular to analyse or predict aspects concerning that natural person's performance at work, ...": the named aspects are examples, so any one of them, and `some other personal aspect`, makes the use an evaluation; the list is read only for whether it is empty.

§ `Article 4(5): pseudonymisation`

-- src:43 | (5) ‘pseudonymisation’ means the processing of personal data in such a manner that the personal data can no longer be attributed to a specific data subject without the use of additional information, provided that such additional information is kept separately and is subject to technical and organisational measures to ensure that the personal data are not attributed to an identified or identifiable natural person;
@ref Art 4(5) 'pseudonymisation' (src:43)
GIVEN `the processing is processing of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal data can no longer be attributed to a specific data subject without the use of additional information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the additional information is kept separately` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the additional information is subject to technical and organisational measures to ensure that the personal data are not attributed to an identified or identifiable natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(5) the processing is pseudonymisation` MEANS
    IF `the processing is processing of personal data`
       AND `the personal data can no longer be attributed to a specific data subject without the use of additional information`
       AND `the additional information is kept separately`
       AND `the additional information is subject to technical and organisational measures to ensure that the personal data are not attributed to an identified or identifiable natural person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the proviso is read as an element of the definition (fork FK4-1), "means the processing of personal data in such a manner that the personal data can no longer be attributed to a specific data subject without the use of additional information, provided that such additional information is kept separately and is subject to technical and organisational measures"

§ `Article 4(9): recipient`

-- src:47 | (9) ‘recipient’ means a natural or legal person, public authority, agency or another body, to which the personal data are disclosed, whether a third party or not. However, public authorities which may receive personal data in the framework of a particular inquiry in accordance with Union or Member State law shall not be regarded as recipients; the processing of those data by those public authorities shall be in compliance with the applicable data protection rules according to the purposes of the processing;
@ref Art 4(9) 'recipient' (src:47)
GIVEN body IS A `Kind of person or body`
      `the personal data are disclosed to the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a third party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal data are received in the framework of a particular inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the receipt is in accordance with Union or Member State law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(9) the body is a recipient` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF body EQUALS `not a person or body`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a natural or legal person, public authority, agency or another body"
        IF NOT (`the personal data are disclosed to the body`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to which the personal data are disclosed"
        IF (body EQUALS `public authority`) AND `the personal data are received in the framework of a particular inquiry` AND `the receipt is in accordance with Union or Member State law`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a flat negative, read as applying to the receipt in the inquiry (fork FK4-2), "public authorities which may receive personal data in the framework of a particular inquiry in accordance with Union or Member State law shall not be regarded as recipients"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
        -- "whether a third party or not": `the body is a third party` is not read, by the text's own words.

-- src:47 | (9) ‘recipient’ means a natural or legal person, public authority, agency or another body, to which the personal data are disclosed, whether a third party or not. However, public authorities which may receive personal data in the framework of a particular inquiry in accordance with Union or Member State law shall not be regarded as recipients; the processing of those data by those public authorities shall be in compliance with the applicable data protection rules according to the purposes of the processing;
@ref Art 4(9) 'recipient': the processing by those public authorities (src:47)
GIVEN body IS A `Kind of person or body`
      `the personal data are received in the framework of a particular inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the receipt is in accordance with Union or Member State law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing complies with the applicable data protection rules according to the purposes of the processing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(9) the processing by the public authority of the data it receives in a particular inquiry is in compliance with the applicable data protection rules` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT ((body EQUALS `public authority`) AND `the personal data are received in the framework of a particular inquiry` AND `the receipt is in accordance with Union or Member State law`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "those public authorities", the ones "which may receive personal data in the framework of a particular inquiry in accordance with Union or Member State law" (fork FK4-3: the duty is read as covering the data received in the inquiry)
        IF `the processing complies with the applicable data protection rules according to the purposes of the processing`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, split site (i)): "the processing of those data by those public authorities shall be in compliance with the applicable data protection rules according to the purposes of the processing"

-- The same sentence as a regulative rule: the text names the party ("those public authorities") and the act
-- (processing in compliance).  It states no time limit and no consequence, so no #TRACE can show it breached
-- (NOTES: Rules with no breach path); none has been invented.
-- src:47 | (9) ‘recipient’ means a natural or legal person, public authority, agency or another body, to which the personal data are disclosed, whether a third party or not. However, public authorities which may receive personal data in the framework of a particular inquiry in accordance with Union or Member State law shall not be regarded as recipients; the processing of those data by those public authorities shall be in compliance with the applicable data protection rules according to the purposes of the processing;
@ref Art 4(9) 'recipient': the duty of those public authorities (src:47)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 4(9) party` `Art 4(9) action`
`Art 4(9) the public authority must process the data it receives in a particular inquiry in compliance with the applicable data protection rules` MEANS
    PARTY `Art 4(9) public authority receiving personal data in a particular inquiry`
    MUST `Art 4(9) process the data in compliance with the applicable data protection rules according to the purposes of the processing`

§ `Article 4(10): third party`

-- src:48 | (10) ‘third party’ means a natural or legal person, public authority, agency or body other than the data subject, controller, processor and persons who, under the direct authority of the controller or processor, are authorised to process personal data;
@ref Art 4(10) 'third party' (src:48)
GIVEN body IS A `Kind of person or body`
      `the body is the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is the processor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a person who, under the direct authority of the controller or processor, is authorised to process personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(10) the body is a third party` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF body EQUALS `not a person or body`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a natural or legal person, public authority, agency or body"
        IF `the body is the data subject` OR `the body is the controller` OR `the body is the processor` OR `the body is a person who, under the direct authority of the controller or processor, is authorised to process personal data`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than the data subject, controller, processor and persons who, under the direct authority of the controller or processor, are authorised to process personal data"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Article 4(11): consent`

-- src:49 | (11) ‘consent’ of the data subject means any freely given, specific, informed and unambiguous indication of the data subject's wishes by which he or she, by a statement or by a clear affirmative action, signifies agreement to the processing of personal data relating to him or her;
@ref Art 4(11) 'consent' (src:49)
GIVEN `the indication is freely given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the indication is specific` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the indication is informed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the indication is unambiguous` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the indication is of the data subject's wishes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `how the data subject signifies agreement` IS A `Art 4(11) how the data subject signifies agreement`
      `the agreement is to the processing of personal data relating to the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(11) the indication is the consent of the data subject` MEANS
    IF `the indication is freely given`
       AND `the indication is specific`
       AND `the indication is informed`
       AND `the indication is unambiguous`
       AND `the indication is of the data subject's wishes`
       AND ((`how the data subject signifies agreement` EQUALS `Art 4(11) by a statement`) OR (`how the data subject signifies agreement` EQUALS `Art 4(11) by a clear affirmative action`))
       AND `the agreement is to the processing of personal data relating to the data subject`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any freely given, specific, informed and unambiguous indication of the data subject's wishes by which he or she, by a statement or by a clear affirmative action, signifies agreement to the processing of personal data relating to him or her"
    -- "freely given", "specific", "informed" and "unambiguous" are judgments the text leaves to the case: each is a plain input.

§ `Article 4(12): personal data breach`

-- src:50 | (12) ‘personal data breach’ means a breach of security leading to the accidental or unlawful destruction, loss, alteration, unauthorised disclosure of, or access to, personal data transmitted, stored or otherwise processed;
@ref Art 4(12) 'personal data breach' (src:50)
GIVEN `there is a breach of security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the breach of security leads to` IS A LIST OF `Art 4(12) consequence of a breach of security`
      `the personal data are transmitted, stored or otherwise processed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(12) the incident is a personal data breach` MEANS
    IF `there is a breach of security`
       AND `the personal data are transmitted, stored or otherwise processed`
       AND any (GIVEN consequence YIELD NOT (consequence EQUALS `Art 4(12) some other consequence`)) `what the breach of security leads to`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a breach of security leading to the accidental or unlawful destruction, loss, alteration, unauthorised disclosure of, or access to, personal data transmitted, stored or otherwise processed"

§ `Article 4(13): genetic data`

-- src:51 | (13) ‘genetic data’ means personal data relating to the inherited or acquired genetic characteristics of a natural person which give unique information about the physiology or the health of that natural person and which result, in particular, from an analysis of a biological sample from the natural person in question;
@ref Art 4(13) 'genetic data' (src:51)
GIVEN `the data are personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data relate to the inherited or acquired genetic characteristics of a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data give unique information about the physiology or the health of that natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data result from an analysis of a biological sample from the natural person in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(13) the data are genetic data` MEANS
    IF `the data are personal data`
       AND `the data relate to the inherited or acquired genetic characteristics of a natural person`
       AND `the data give unique information about the physiology or the health of that natural person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means personal data relating to the inherited or acquired genetic characteristics of a natural person which give unique information about the physiology or the health of that natural person"
    -- "which result, in particular, from an analysis of a biological sample": read as an example of where the data come from, so `the data result from an analysis of a biological sample from the natural person in question` is not read (fork FK4-4).

§ `Article 4(14): biometric data`

-- src:52 | (14) ‘biometric data’ means personal data resulting from specific technical processing relating to the physical, physiological or behavioural characteristics of a natural person, which allow or confirm the unique identification of that natural person, such as facial images or dactyloscopic data;
@ref Art 4(14) 'biometric data' (src:52)
GIVEN `the data are personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data result from specific technical processing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data relate to the physical, physiological or behavioural characteristics of a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data allow or confirm the unique identification of that natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data are facial images or dactyloscopic data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(14) the data are biometric data` MEANS
    IF `the data are personal data`
       AND `the data result from specific technical processing`
       AND `the data relate to the physical, physiological or behavioural characteristics of a natural person`
       AND `the data allow or confirm the unique identification of that natural person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means personal data resulting from specific technical processing relating to the physical, physiological or behavioural characteristics of a natural person, which allow or confirm the unique identification of that natural person"
    -- "such as facial images or dactyloscopic data": examples, so `the data are facial images or dactyloscopic data` is not read, by the text's own words.

§ `Article 4(15): data concerning health`

-- src:53 | (15) ‘data concerning health’ means personal data related to the physical or mental health of a natural person, including the provision of health care services, which reveal information about his or her health status;
@ref Art 4(15) 'data concerning health' (src:53)
GIVEN `the data are personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data relate to the physical or mental health of a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data relate to the provision of health care services to the natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data reveal information about the health status of the natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(15) the data are data concerning health` MEANS
    IF `the data are personal data`
       AND (`the data relate to the physical or mental health of a natural person` OR `the data relate to the provision of health care services to the natural person`)
       AND `the data reveal information about the health status of the natural person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means personal data related to the physical or mental health of a natural person, including the provision of health care services, which reveal information about his or her health status"
    -- "which reveal information about his or her health status" is read as qualifying the personal data, both limbs (fork FK4-5).
    -- "including the provision of health care services": data about the provision of health care services count as related to health, so either of the two relations suffices; the clause "which reveal information about his or her health status" is required for both.

§ `Article 4(13) to (15): the categories of Article 9(1) that these three definitions give`

-- The categories of Art 9(1) that P1's choice `Art 9(1) category of personal data` names and that Art 4(13), (14) and (15)
-- define are genetic data, biometric data and data concerning health.  The functions below answer P1's choice from the
-- three answers above.  The other five categories of Art 9(1) (racial or ethnic origin, political opinions, religious or
-- philosophical beliefs, trade union membership, sex life or sexual orientation) are not defined in Art 4 and are not
-- decided here.
-- src:51 | (13) ‘genetic data’ means personal data relating to the inherited or acquired genetic characteristics of a natural person which give unique information about the physiology or the health of that natural person and which result, in particular, from an analysis of a biological sample from the natural person in question;
-- src:52 | (14) ‘biometric data’ means personal data resulting from specific technical processing relating to the physical, physiological or behavioural characteristics of a natural person, which allow or confirm the unique identification of that natural person, such as facial images or dactyloscopic data;
-- src:53 | (15) ‘data concerning health’ means personal data related to the physical or mental health of a natural person, including the provision of health care services, which reveal information about his or her health status;
@ref Art 4(13), (14), (15) feeding Art 9(1) (src:51-53)
GIVEN `the data are genetic data` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the data are biometric data` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the biometric data are processed for the purpose of uniquely identifying a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data are data concerning health` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Art 9(1) category of personal data`)
`Art 4(13) to (15) the categories of Article 9(1) that the data fall in by these definitions` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the data are genetic data` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the data are biometric data` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the data are data concerning health` EQUALS NOTHING)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): at least one of the three definitions, "means personal data relating to the inherited or acquired genetic characteristics", "means personal data resulting from specific technical processing" or "means personal data related to the physical or mental health of a natural person", gives no answer, so the list is not decided whatever the other two answer: a definition that is met would be listed, but one that gives no answer may be met too (fork FK4-6)
        IF (`the data are genetic data` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`the data are biometric data` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`the data are data concerning health` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST EMPTY
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): each of the three definitions "means" its term, and none is met, so none of the three categories is given; this says nothing of the five categories of Art 9(1) that Art 4 does not define
        -- every answer is JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE and at least one is JUST TRUE: the list names each category whose definition is met, in the order genetic, biometric, health
        OTHERWISE JUST (append
                            (IF `the data are genetic data` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN LIST `Art 9(1) genetic data` ELSE EMPTY)
                            (append
                                (IF `the data are biometric data` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                                 THEN (IF `the biometric data are processed for the purpose of uniquely identifying a natural person`
                                       THEN LIST `Art 9(1) biometric data for the purpose of uniquely identifying a natural person`
                                       ELSE LIST `Art 9(1) biometric data not for the purpose of uniquely identifying a natural person`)
                                 ELSE EMPTY)
                                (IF `the data are data concerning health` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN LIST `Art 9(1) data concerning health` ELSE EMPTY)))

-- src:51 | (13) ‘genetic data’ means personal data relating to the inherited or acquired genetic characteristics of a natural person which give unique information about the physiology or the health of that natural person and which result, in particular, from an analysis of a biological sample from the natural person in question;
-- src:52 | (14) ‘biometric data’ means personal data resulting from specific technical processing relating to the physical, physiological or behavioural characteristics of a natural person, which allow or confirm the unique identification of that natural person, such as facial images or dactyloscopic data;
-- src:53 | (15) ‘data concerning health’ means personal data related to the physical or mental health of a natural person, including the provision of health care services, which reveal information about his or her health status;
@ref Art 4(13), (14), (15) feeding Art 9(1): the single choice (src:51-53)
GIVEN `the data are genetic data` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the data are biometric data` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the biometric data are processed for the purpose of uniquely identifying a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data are data concerning health` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Art 9(1) category of personal data`
`Art 4(13) to (15) the category of Article 9(1) that the data fall in by these definitions` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the data are genetic data` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST `Art 9(1) genetic data`
        IF (`the data are biometric data` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the biometric data are processed for the purpose of uniquely identifying a natural person`
        THEN JUST `Art 9(1) biometric data for the purpose of uniquely identifying a natural person`
        IF `the data are biometric data` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST `Art 9(1) biometric data not for the purpose of uniquely identifying a natural person`
        IF `the data are data concerning health` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST `Art 9(1) data concerning health`
        -- any one definition that is met brings the data into a category of Art 9(1), whatever the other two answer; when more than one is met the first in the order genetic, biometric, health is taken (fork FK4-6)
        IF (`the data are genetic data` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`the data are biometric data` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`the data are data concerning health` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): none of "means personal data relating to the inherited or acquired genetic characteristics", "means personal data resulting from specific technical processing" and "means personal data related to the physical or mental health of a natural person" is met, so the data may still be in one of the five categories of Art 9(1) that Art 4 does not define, or in none (fork FK4-6)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): at least one of the three definitions "means personal data relating to the inherited or acquired genetic characteristics", "means personal data resulting from specific technical processing" or "means personal data related to the physical or mental health of a natural person" gives no answer and none is met

§ `Article 4(16): main establishment`

-- src:54 | (16) ‘main establishment’ means:
-- src:55 | (a) as regards a controller with establishments in more than one Member State, the place of its central administration in the Union, unless the decisions on the purposes and means of the processing of personal data are taken in another establishment of the controller in the Union and the latter establishment has the power to have such decisions implemented, in which case the establishment having taken such decisions is to be considered to be the main establishment;
@ref Art 4(16)(a) 'main establishment' of a controller (src:54-55)
GIVEN `the controller has establishments in more than one Member State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller's central administration is in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decisions on the purposes and means of the processing are taken in another establishment of the controller in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that other establishment has the power to have such decisions implemented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Art 4(16) which establishment is the main establishment`
`Art 4(16)(a) the main establishment of a controller` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the controller has establishments in more than one Member State`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as regards a controller with establishments in more than one Member State"
        IF `the decisions on the purposes and means of the processing are taken in another establishment of the controller in the Union` AND `that other establishment has the power to have such decisions implemented`
        THEN JUST `Art 4(16)(a) the establishment of the controller that took the decisions on the purposes and means`
        IF `the controller's central administration is in the Union`
        THEN JUST `Art 4(16)(a) the place of the controller's central administration in the Union`
        -- the "unless" is not met unless both limbs hold: decisions taken elsewhere without the power to have them implemented leave the central administration the main establishment
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names only "the place of its central administration in the Union", and the controller has none there and the exception does not hold

-- src:54 | (16) ‘main establishment’ means:
-- src:56 | (b) as regards a processor with establishments in more than one Member State, the place of its central administration in the Union, or, if the processor has no central administration in the Union, the establishment of the processor in the Union where the main processing activities in the context of the activities of an establishment of the processor take place to the extent that the processor is subject to specific obligations under this Regulation;
@ref Art 4(16)(b) 'main establishment' of a processor (src:54-56)
GIVEN `the processor has establishments in more than one Member State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processor has a central administration in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processor has an establishment in the Union where the main processing activities in the context of the activities of an establishment of the processor take place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processor is subject to specific obligations under this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Art 4(16) which establishment is the main establishment`
`Art 4(16)(b) the main establishment of a processor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the processor has establishments in more than one Member State`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as regards a processor with establishments in more than one Member State"
        IF `the processor has a central administration in the Union`
        THEN JUST `Art 4(16)(b) the place of the processor's central administration in the Union`
        IF `the processor has an establishment in the Union where the main processing activities in the context of the activities of an establishment of the processor take place` AND `the processor is subject to specific obligations under this Regulation`
        THEN JUST `Art 4(16)(b) the establishment of the processor in the Union where the main processing activities take place`
        IF `the processor has an establishment in the Union where the main processing activities in the context of the activities of an establishment of the processor take place`
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the extent that the processor is subject to specific obligations under this Regulation"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the processor has no central administration in the Union and no establishment in the Union where the main processing activities take place, and the text says nothing for that case

§ `Article 4(17): representative`

-- src:57 | (17) ‘representative’ means a natural or legal person established in the Union who, designated by the controller or processor in writing pursuant to Article 27, represents the controller or processor with regard to their respective obligations under this Regulation;
@ref Art 4(17) 'representative' (src:57)
GIVEN person IS A `Kind of person or body`
      `the person is established in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is designated by the controller or processor in writing pursuant to Article 27` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person represents the controller or processor with regard to their respective obligations under this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(17) the person is a representative` MEANS
    IF ((person EQUALS `natural person`) OR (person EQUALS `legal person`))
       AND `the person is established in the Union`
       AND `the person is designated by the controller or processor in writing pursuant to Article 27`
       AND `the person represents the controller or processor with regard to their respective obligations under this Regulation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a natural or legal person established in the Union who, designated by the controller or processor in writing pursuant to Article 27, represents the controller or processor with regard to their respective obligations under this Regulation"

§ `Article 4(18): enterprise`

-- src:58 | (18) ‘enterprise’ means a natural or legal person engaged in an economic activity, irrespective of its legal form, including partnerships or associations regularly engaged in an economic activity;
@ref Art 4(18) 'enterprise' (src:58)
GIVEN body IS A `Kind of person or body`
      `the body is engaged in an economic activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a partnership or an association` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the partnership or association is regularly engaged in an economic activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(18) the body is an enterprise` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF body EQUALS `not a person or body`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a natural or legal person engaged in an economic activity"
        IF `the body is a partnership or an association` AND `the partnership or association is regularly engaged in an economic activity`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF ((body EQUALS `natural person`) OR (body EQUALS `legal person`)) AND `the body is engaged in an economic activity`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- "irrespective of its legal form": the answer does not depend on the form of the natural or legal person.
        IF (body EQUALS `natural person`) OR (body EQUALS `legal person`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a natural or legal person engaged in an economic activity"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): fork FK4-7; "including partnerships or associations regularly engaged in an economic activity" shows that the term reaches beyond natural and legal persons, and the text does not say whether another body, or a partnership or association that is not regularly engaged, is an enterprise

§ `Article 4(19): group of undertakings`

-- src:59 | (19) ‘group of undertakings’ means a controlling undertaking and its controlled undertakings;
@ref Art 4(19) 'group of undertakings' (src:59)
GIVEN `an undertaking in the set is a controlling undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every other undertaking in the set is controlled by that controlling undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(19) the set of undertakings is a group of undertakings` MEANS
    IF `an undertaking in the set is a controlling undertaking` AND `every other undertaking in the set is controlled by that controlling undertaking`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a controlling undertaking and its controlled undertakings"
    -- "controlling undertaking" and "controlled undertakings" are not defined in the text: each is a plain input.

§ `Article 4(20): binding corporate rules`

-- src:60 | (20) ‘binding corporate rules’ means personal data protection policies which are adhered to by a controller or processor established on the territory of a Member State for transfers or a set of transfers of personal data to a controller or processor in one or more third countries within a group of undertakings, or group of enterprises engaged in a joint economic activity;
@ref Art 4(20) 'binding corporate rules' (src:60)
GIVEN `the rules are personal data protection policies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the policies are adhered to by a controller or processor established on the territory of a Member State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the policies are for transfers or a set of transfers of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfers are to a controller or processor in one or more third countries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfers are within a group of undertakings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfers are within a group of enterprises engaged in a joint economic activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(20) the policies are binding corporate rules` MEANS
    IF `the rules are personal data protection policies`
       AND `the policies are adhered to by a controller or processor established on the territory of a Member State`
       AND `the policies are for transfers or a set of transfers of personal data`
       AND `the transfers are to a controller or processor in one or more third countries`
       AND (`the transfers are within a group of undertakings` OR `the transfers are within a group of enterprises engaged in a joint economic activity`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means personal data protection policies which are adhered to by a controller or processor established on the territory of a Member State for transfers or a set of transfers of personal data to a controller or processor in one or more third countries within a group of undertakings, or group of enterprises engaged in a joint economic activity"

§ `Article 4(21): supervisory authority`

-- src:61 | (21) ‘supervisory authority’ means an independent public authority which is established by a Member State pursuant to Article 51;
@ref Art 4(21) 'supervisory authority' (src:61)
GIVEN body IS A `Kind of person or body`
      `the body is independent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is established by a Member State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is established pursuant to Article 51` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(21) the body is a supervisory authority` MEANS
    IF (body EQUALS `public authority`)
       AND `the body is independent`
       AND `the body is established by a Member State`
       AND `the body is established pursuant to Article 51`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means an independent public authority which is established by a Member State pursuant to Article 51"

§ `Article 4(22): supervisory authority concerned`

-- src:62 | (22) ‘supervisory authority concerned’ means a supervisory authority which is concerned by the processing of personal data because:
-- src:63 | (a) the controller or processor is established on the territory of the Member State of that supervisory authority;
-- src:64 | (b) data subjects residing in the Member State of that supervisory authority are substantially affected or likely to be substantially affected by the processing; or
-- src:65 | (c) a complaint has been lodged with that supervisory authority;
@ref Art 4(22)(a), (b), (c) 'supervisory authority concerned' (src:62-65)
GIVEN `the body is a supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller or processor is established on the territory of the Member State of that supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `data subjects residing in the Member State of that supervisory authority are substantially affected by the processing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `data subjects residing in the Member State of that supervisory authority are likely to be substantially affected by the processing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a complaint has been lodged with that supervisory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(22) the supervisory authority is a supervisory authority concerned by the processing` MEANS
    IF `the body is a supervisory authority`
       AND (`the controller or processor is established on the territory of the Member State of that supervisory authority`
            OR `data subjects residing in the Member State of that supervisory authority are substantially affected by the processing`
            OR `data subjects residing in the Member State of that supervisory authority are likely to be substantially affected by the processing`
            OR `a complaint has been lodged with that supervisory authority`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a supervisory authority which is concerned by the processing of personal data because"

§ `Article 4(23): cross-border processing`

-- src:66 | (23) ‘cross-border processing’ means either:
-- src:67 | (a) processing of personal data which takes place in the context of the activities of establishments in more than one Member State of a controller or processor in the Union where the controller or processor is established in more than one Member State; or
-- src:68 | (b) processing of personal data which takes place in the context of the activities of a single establishment of a controller or processor in the Union but which substantially affects or is likely to substantially affect data subjects in more than one Member State.
@ref Art 4(23)(a), (b) 'cross-border processing' (src:66-68)
GIVEN `the processing is processing of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing takes place in the context of the activities of establishments in more than one Member State of a controller or processor in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller or processor is established in more than one Member State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing takes place in the context of the activities of a single establishment of a controller or processor in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing substantially affects data subjects in more than one Member State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is likely to substantially affect data subjects in more than one Member State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(23) the processing is cross-border processing` MEANS
    IF `the processing is processing of personal data`
       AND ((`the processing takes place in the context of the activities of establishments in more than one Member State of a controller or processor in the Union`
             AND `the controller or processor is established in more than one Member State`)
            OR (`the processing takes place in the context of the activities of a single establishment of a controller or processor in the Union`
                AND (`the processing substantially affects data subjects in more than one Member State` OR `the processing is likely to substantially affect data subjects in more than one Member State`)))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means either: (a) processing of personal data which takes place in the context of the activities of establishments in more than one Member State of a controller or processor in the Union where the controller or processor is established in more than one Member State; or (b) processing of personal data which takes place in the context of the activities of a single establishment of a controller or processor in the Union but which substantially affects or is likely to substantially affect data subjects in more than one Member State"

§ `Article 4(24): relevant and reasoned objection`

-- src:69 | (24) ‘relevant and reasoned objection’ means an objection to a draft decision as to whether there is an infringement of this Regulation, or whether envisaged action in relation to the controller or processor complies with this Regulation, which clearly demonstrates the significance of the risks posed by the draft decision as regards the fundamental rights and freedoms of data subjects and, where applicable, the free flow of personal data within the Union;
@ref Art 4(24) 'relevant and reasoned objection' (src:69)
GIVEN `the objection is to a draft decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the objection is as to whether there is an infringement of this Regulation, or whether envisaged action in relation to the controller or processor complies with this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the objection clearly demonstrates the significance of the risks posed by the draft decision as regards the fundamental rights and freedoms of data subjects` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the free flow of personal data within the Union is at issue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the objection clearly demonstrates the significance of the risks posed by the draft decision as regards the free flow of personal data within the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(24) the objection is a relevant and reasoned objection` MEANS
    IF `the objection is to a draft decision`
       AND `the objection is as to whether there is an infringement of this Regulation, or whether envisaged action in relation to the controller or processor complies with this Regulation`
       AND `the objection clearly demonstrates the significance of the risks posed by the draft decision as regards the fundamental rights and freedoms of data subjects`
       AND ((NOT (`the free flow of personal data within the Union is at issue`)) OR `the objection clearly demonstrates the significance of the risks posed by the draft decision as regards the free flow of personal data within the Union`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means an objection to a draft decision as to whether there is an infringement of this Regulation, or whether envisaged action in relation to the controller or processor complies with this Regulation, which clearly demonstrates the significance of the risks posed by the draft decision as regards the fundamental rights and freedoms of data subjects and, where applicable, the free flow of personal data within the Union"
    -- "where applicable": a failed "where" gate is the text's no (periods ruling (b)); the free flow is not asked when it is not at issue.

§ `Article 4(25): information society service`

-- src:70 | (25) ‘information society service’ means a service as defined in point (b) of Article 1(1) of Directive (EU) 2015/1535 of the European Parliament and of the Council (
-- src:71 | [^1]
@ref Art 4(25) 'information society service' (src:70-71)
GIVEN `the service is a service as defined in point (b) of Article 1(1) of Directive (EU) 2015/1535` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(25) the service is an information society service` MEANS
    IF `the service is a service as defined in point (b) of Article 1(1) of Directive (EU) 2015/1535`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a service as defined in point (b) of Article 1(1) of Directive (EU) 2015/1535"
    -- The Directive is not among the sources and is not encoded: whether a service is "as defined in" it is the borrowed fact, asked as a plain input.

§ `Article 4(26): international organisation`

-- src:73 | (26) ‘international organisation’ means an organisation and its subordinate bodies governed by public international law, or any other body which is set up by, or on the basis of, an agreement between two or more countries.
