GIVEN `the body is an organisation governed by public international law, or a subordinate body of such an organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is another body set up by, or on the basis of, an agreement between two or more countries` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(26) the body is an international organisation` MEANS
    IF `the body is an organisation governed by public international law, or a subordinate body of such an organisation` OR `the body is another body set up by, or on the basis of, an agreement between two or more countries`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means an organisation and its subordinate bodies governed by public international law, or any other body which is set up by, or on the basis of, an agreement between two or more countries"
